  "worked_solution": "For a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S,$ we can calculate the expected value using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]={\\int }_{S}x\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\n \n\nWe compute the expected value of $X$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & ={\\int }_{0}^{e}x\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}x\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{e}x\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}x\\cdot \\frac{6x}{5}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{e}x\\cdot \\frac{2}{5x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{6{x}^{2}}{5}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{e}\\frac{2}{5}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{2{x}^{3}}{5}|}_{0}^{1}+{\\frac{2x}{5}|}_{1}^{e} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{5}+\\frac{2e}{5}-\\frac{2}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{2e}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
